13. Design and Engineering Rules
Tech Stack: Build using a clean, modular, maintainable Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + Lucide Icons architecture (or clean Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS if static export is preferred—configure next.config with output: 'export' compatibility so it can be hosted independently on any cloud/CDN infrastructure outside Framer).

Component Architecture: Separate data arrays (services, fleet specs, industries, FAQs, portal telemetry previews) into dedicated typed configuration files so copy updates never require touching JSX layout logic.

Zero External UI Bloat: Use semantic HTML5 (<header>, <main>, <section>, <nav>, <footer>), native CSS Grid/Flexbox, and lightweight custom SVG components.

Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA): Maintain 4.5:1+ contrast ratios across both Dark and Light themes, visible :focus-visible outlines (2px solid #2E90FA), proper heading hierarchy (h1 -> h2 -> h3), and descriptive aria-label attributes on icon buttons and phone links.

